{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-127510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/e0d18f7db92cfbe372f998e69d2395f2d586eb36cd25773588149c4ccf678eba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,6).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(3,6)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=12x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{6}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be5afdc44f26125b7c0dcde6547b19d299f3f8fd0dc1406db4ffd52a4db4e25"} {"question" "q-127510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{6y}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2y}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/60987d053d138d4a26cbc05adccb0da23810f97243f9399d3fe401a0202394b0.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-8,4).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-8$ and $y=4$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 16 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be5afdc44f26125b7c0dcde6547b19d299f3f8fd0dc1406db4ffd52a4db4e25"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{y}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4y}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/ebef81911a434828ab94e643007d06b677538cdf0995198c7a065e35a8f81996.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{4}+2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be5afdc44f26125b7c0dcde6547b19d299f3f8fd0dc1406db4ffd52a4db4e25"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{4(x+1)}{y+1}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4(y+1)}{x+1}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-1}{4(y-1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{y-1}{4(x-1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/eb0fbc8f57621946a5ec5168e8c607d230269e0c6a64b4c86c835c110f0f6288.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our ellipse is centered at $(0,1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be5afdc44f26125b7c0dcde6547b19d299f3f8fd0dc1406db4ffd52a4db4e25"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{4(y-1)}{9x}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3(y-1)}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{3x}{2(y-1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4x}{9(y-1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-127525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-342355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/assets/1aab10c5376ca6ae6c43829bc6f7617fb236b24c883d8ad61c47b83b75511d5a.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-342355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(6,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=6$ and $y=-2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 4 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{2}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-342355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7be5afdc44f26125b7c0dcde6547b19d299f3f8fd0dc1406db4ffd52a4db4e25"} {"question" "q-342355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"} {"question" "q-342355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069054/state.json" "file_sha256" "30705cb6fc4d83eb6d679bcf59da3bd8ba21cd17f5c87f6843a49738ce70c908"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2334 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
